// A tall cave, acid at its foot; a ladder of ledges, some of them crumbling, past a rising ember; a shelf with spouts; two pits with stones against their far walls; the door high on the far wall.
name Ashfall
rule B1234/S012345678
steps 3
hint Climb the ledges; a seed lies on one, some of them fall, and an ember rises and falls between them. Above: a shelf with vents, a pit with a stone and an ember, a second seed, a second pit. Two blooms, one after the other, up to the door.
tip Each pit's bloom was cut by the pit's far wall: the stone is one cell from that wall, not in the middle. Grow the first, fetch the second seed, plant, climb out, rewind, grow both from the ledge.
intro The cave climbs, and what is under it is green and does not forgive. Ledge by ledge, with an ember rising and falling in the dark between them.
outro You climbed through the dark and grew a stair at the top of it. The way down is behind you now.
say wake|Look down. Now do not look down again.
say seed|One seed. There is another, higher.
say plant|Against the wall of the pit. The wall will take a third of the bloom; the rest is yours.
say grow|Three generations. Stand on the rim, not in it.
say found|Stair by stair. The door is at the top.
say die|Falling is quick. Climbing is not. Climb.
